==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-}}
From {{bor|en|fr|acide}}, from {{der|en|la|acidus||sour, acid}}, from {{m|la|aceō||I am sour}}. {{doublet|en|agita}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{enPR|ăs'ĭd}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈæsɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-acid.ogg|Audio (GA)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æsɪd|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|acider}}

# [[sour|Sour]], [[sharp]], or [[biting]] to the taste; [[tart]]; having the taste of [[vinegar]].
#: {{ux|en|'''acid''' fruits or liquors}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Sour-[[tempered]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1864|author=w:Anthony Trollope|title=w:The Small House at Allington|publisher=Smith, Elder & Co.|edition=2nd|volume=2|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=smkOAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA235&dq=%22his+face+as+acid+as+ever%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwioq7KQ5bHbAhVEWrwKHZaGAKgQ6AEIJzAA#v=onepage&q=%22his%20face%20as%20acid%20as%20ever%22&f=false|page=235
|passage=His voice was as stern and his face as '''acid''' as ever.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage=It must be admitted that Challenger is provocative in the last degree, but Summerlee has an '''acid''' tongue, which makes matters worse.}}
#* {{RQ:Vance Nobody|I
|passage=Little disappointed, then, she turned attention to "Chat of the Social World," gossip which exercised potent fascination upon the girl's intelligence. She devoured with more avidity than she had her food those pretentiously phrased chronicles of the snobocracy {{...}} distilling therefrom an '''acid''' envy that robbed her napoleon of all its savour.}}
# Of or pertaining to an acid; [[acidic]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1975|author=Peter N. Barber; Cecil Ernest Lucas Phillips|title=The Trees Around Us|page=101
|passage=Like other nyssas, it is in nature a creature of swampy places and looks loveliest where massed close to water and reflected in it, but justifies itself elsewhere if the soil is moist and '''acid''', succeeding in wet clay.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} Denoting a musical [[genre]] that is a distortion (as if hallucinogenic) of an existing genre, as in [[acid house]], [[acid jazz]], [[acid rock]].

