===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[sour]] substance.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}}
## Any compound which yields [[H+]] ions ([[proton]]s) when dissolved in [[water]]; an [[Arrhenius acid]].
## Any compound that easily [[donate]]s [[proton]]s to a [[base]]; a [[Brønsted acid]].
## Any compound that can [[accept]] a pair of [[electron]]s to form a [[covalent bond]]; a [[Lewis acid]].
# Any [[corrosive]] substance.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=James Fenton|title=Jerusalem
|passage=You are in error. / This is terror. / This is your banishment. This land is mine. / This is what you earn. / This is the Law of No Return. / This is the sour dough, this the sweet wine. / This is my history, this my race / And this unhappy man threw '''acid''' in my face.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} [[LSD]], [[lysergic acid diethylamide]].
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Joe David Brown|title=The Hippies|year=1967|publisher=Time, Inc|location=New York|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/hippies00brow/page/171/mode/1up|page=171|passage=In the end, though, there is one sure way to distinguish a real hippie from his assorted sympathizers: hippies drop '''acid'''. That is, real hippies frequently, if irregularly, ingest LSD.}}

